WEBVTT

00:00:02.639 --> 00:00:06.879
a useful feature within word

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.600
is the ability to merge the contents of

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:09.519
a letter

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.960
with the database of clients names and

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:12.719
addresses

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.160
in this example i'm going to use the

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:15.360
files that you can download from the

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.279
vision alone website

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.359
to show how you can link the names and

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:21.520
addresses of four clients

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:23.359
to the letter which can then be sent out

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.279
without having to type out each

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:29.359
individual person's names and addresses

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:31.039
so the first thing i need to do is open

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:32.079
the letter which i have done on the

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.040
screen there

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:36.960
and to access the mail merge tool i need

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.040
to go to the mailings tab so if i click

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.719
on the mailings tab

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.079
this brings up a range of options and

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:43.840
the tool we're going to use here is the

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:45.360
mail merge wizard so if i click on the

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.360
start meal merge

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.280
and select the step-by-step mail merge

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.520
wizard

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.280
that will then bring up the dialog box

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.719
on the right hand side

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.960
now there are six steps in the mail

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:58.480
merge process and we'll work through

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.960
each one individually

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.640
so the first one is select document type

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.720
so what type of document are you working

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.320
on well we're working on a letter

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:10.400
so we're happy with that and step two

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.159
and select the starting document so how

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.840
do you want to set up your letters

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:15.840
and again we're going to use the first

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.240
option here is use the current document

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.680
you could go from a template and start

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.400
from an existing document that's

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.400
somewhere else

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.840
so we'll now move to step three now at

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.799
this point this is where you're going to

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.880
link the letter

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:32.000
with the data source so what you need to

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.840
do is you need to browse

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.280
to the location where you see if the

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.920
spreadsheet containing the names and

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.560
addresses

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.159
downloaded so i'll save these and my

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.240
documents folder

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:44.000
in the it course and in the word

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.600
processing folder

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.040
and you will see this as an excel

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.439
spreadsheet and it is sample

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.439
mail merge addresses so i just simply

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:53.600
double click on that

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:55.439
and that then gives me the option so

00:01:53.600 --> 00:02:00.240
it's asking me to select a table

00:01:55.439 --> 00:02:01.600
and i'm happy with that i click ok

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.000
this then brings up the mail merge

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.159
recipients dialog box so this tells me

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.039
what the contents of the spreadsheet are

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:10.560
so i know there are four people within

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:12.480
that spreadsheet and the names and

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.400
addresses are all there

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.000
if i didn't want to send the letter to a

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.319
specific person i can

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
tick or untick that box and it will

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:22.879
remove them it won't include them

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.599
in the merge and when i'm happy with

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.680
that i click ok

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:28.800
and it is now time to move on to the

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.400
next step

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.840
so if i go to step four

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.760
this is about right your letter so if

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.440
you hadn't already done so at this point

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.040
you would write the letter

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.959
but what we need to do now is the letter

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.959
is already written so we simply need to

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:44.160
insert the address block and the

00:02:42.959 --> 00:02:46.879
greeting line

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.720
so the address block is traditionally

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:49.519
inserted at the top left-hand section of

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.840
the letter

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:53.760
so i will place the cursor there where i

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.000
want the address block to appear

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.000
and if i look along to the right if i

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.239
click on address block

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.920
i then have the insert address block

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:04.159
dialog box

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.000
in here it will show me what the

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:07.680
addresses will look like

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.120
there are four recipients on the off so

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.159
it will then preview

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.599
each one and i'm happy with that so i

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:16.239
can then

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:17.040
select okay so it will insert the

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:19.280
address block

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.319
merge field i'm also going to add the

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.080
greeting line

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:24.239
and the greeting line would be just

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.200
above the main body of text so i'll

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:28.640
place the cursor there and select

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.480
reading line

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.040
again this will give me a dialog box

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.599
which shows me a demonstration of a

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.280
preview

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:40.000
of what will be seen on the letter

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:41.760
if i'm happy with that i click ok and

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.920
that inserts it reading

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.200
so now what we need to do is we need to

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.879
preview the letters

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.400
so i click on step five

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:52.080
you can see that the address block and

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.080
the greeting line have changed and

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.680
are now the full names and addresses of

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.840
the people

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:01.840
again i can preview each of the letters

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.840
to see that i'm happy with it

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.959
i can't exclude recipients or i can even

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.560
edit the recipient list at this point

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:12.720
so the final step would be to complete

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:14.959
the merge and if i selected print

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:19.600
i can then select all and i could print

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:19.600
out the letters